INT. LIGHTHOUSE GALLEY - POTLUCK NIGHT

A cramped round kitchen at the base of a lighthouse. Casserole dishes crowd every surface. A foghorn blares every ten seconds.

ROSALIND (60s, apron, vengeful smile) guards a bundt cake. EDMUND (60s, golf shirt) carves a ham. CHIKA (30s, nose ring, crisp linen) pours wine. DMITRI (40s, ponytail, guitar case) leans on the counter. BEA (20s, headphones around neck) scrolls her phone.

ROSALIND
I'm only saying that some of us brought homemade.

EDMUND
Rosalind, it's the same casserole you brought to the last four potlucks.

ROSALIND
It's a family recipe.

CHIKA
It's from a can.

DMITRI
Cream of mushroom. I smelled it in the parking lot.

BEA
Aunt Rosalind, are you aware you're yelling?

ROSALIND
I am explaining.

EDMUND
Over the foghorn.

ROSALIND
Because I'm tired of being the villain in this lighthouse!

CHIKA
Nobody said villain.

DMITRI
I said cannibal. The cake looks human.

ROSALIND
It's a bundt!

EDMUND
Honey, put the knife down.

ROSALIND
This is a cake server!

BEA
It's honestly a very sharp cake server.

The door bangs open. AUNT FENELLA (80s, fur stole, cane held like a spear) sweeps in, trailing mist. Everyone stops.

AUNT FENELLA
I'm told someone has been slandering my casserole.

ROSALIND
Your casserole?

AUNT FENELLA
Cream of mushroom, 1974. I invented it at this very counter.

EDMUND
Nobody told us that.

CHIKA
Why would anyone tell us that?

DMITRI
Because they're afraid of her.

AUNT FENELLA
Quite right.

BEA
I'm getting cake.

ROSALIND
(whispering)
Nobody touch the cake.
